,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ff08f75f2fe5fe10b333696fe5e07677279dd4067d7354554b9c4bb27ff91ae6.bin","sha256":"ff08f75f2fe5fe10b333696fe5e07677279dd4067d7354554b9c4bb27ff91ae6"}},{"id":"644688a8b25781fa937bd2bea8345256a78ff9a1a58f26225aa42b718aaa5fd2","quote":"Our ability to develop new customers’ network and retain existing customers","context":"Our business and operating results are influenced by general factors that affect the industry we are in, including economic and political conditions, the evolving needs of investors, changes in demand for our services and changes in financial conditions and appetite of our current and potential customers. In addition, the following company-specific factors can affect our results of operations materially:","section":"Factors Affecting Our Results of Operations","block":11,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ff08f75f2fe5fe10b333696fe5e07677279dd4067d7354554b9c4bb27ff91ae6.bin","sha256":"ff08f75f2fe5fe10b333696fe5e07677279dd4067d7354554b9c4bb27ff91ae6"}},{"id":"a8fe44f663dfdb7e777f93172703b81ae56c3509be4765256fc028aabedadee2","quote":"Our revenue largely depends on our ability to develop new customer networks and retain existing ones. Our services are negotiated on a project-by-project basis, leading to potential fluctuations in revenue. There is also no assurance that the customers which have previously sought our services will continue to retain us for future businesses. Therefore, our future financial results may be subject to fluctuations depending on our success in entering into new engagements.","context":"Our ability to develop new customers’ network and retain existing customers","section":"Factors Affecting Our Results of Operations","block":12,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ff08f75f2fe5fe10b333696fe5e07677279dd4067d7354554b9c4bb27ff91ae6.bin","sha256":"ff08f75f2fe5fe10b333696fe5e07677279dd4067d7354554b9c4bb27ff91ae6"}},{"id":"a02493f5c21393d18b74ef956c628a1d0496c66133e3c37b7831679172c75572","quote":"Our ability to adapt to rapid technological change and adopt new technology","context":"Our revenue largely depends on our ability to develop new customer networks and retain existing ones. Our services are negotiated on a project-by-project basis, leading to potential fluctuations in revenue. There is also no assurance that the customers which have previously sought our services will continue to retain us for future businesses. Therefore, our future financial results may be subject to fluctuations depending on our success in entering into new engagements.","section":"Factors Affecting Our Results of Operations","block":13,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ff08f75f2fe5fe10b333696fe5e07677279dd4067d7354554b9c4bb27ff91ae6.bin","sha256":"ff08f75f2fe5fe10b333696fe5e07677279dd4067d7354554b9c4bb27ff91ae6"}},{"id":"f12152a9c36f5294eb65b7faefcc224db5da42e9d9515e2a1ccc4220c35972a3","quote":"The general market and industry are rapidly changing technologically, with highly evolving industry standards and frequent introductions and enhancements of new products and services. Customers also expect fast technological advancements. Our future success depends on our ability to adapt to these rapidly changing technologies, align our services with evolving industry standards, and continually improve the know-how of our staff in response to the evolving demands of the marketplace. We are engaged in brokering and providing fintech services to our customers, and the success of the business hinges on our ability to continue adapting to evolving technology and finding our edge in the market. Staying ahead of technological advancements and integrating innovative solutions into our services is crucial for maintaining our competitive position. Failure to adapt to technological changes and effectively adopt new technology could result in a loss of market share and adversely affect our business, financial condition, and results of operations.","context":"Our ability to adapt to rapid technological change and adopt new technology","section":"Factors Affecting Our Results of Operations","block":14,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ff08f75f2fe5fe10b333696fe5e07677279dd4067d7354554b9c4bb27ff91ae6.bin","sha256":"ff08f75f2fe5fe10b333696fe5e07677279dd4067d7354554b9c4bb27ff91ae6"}},{"id":"4bb518e23d56b985d9969e2d3b65f8650ce61500ca9e6d40cbb46c93d201661b","quote":"Our ability to retain employees who have strong relationships with our customers","context":"The general market and industry are rapidly changing technologically, with highly evolving industry standards and frequent introductions and enhancements of new products and services. Customers also expect fast technological advancements. Our future success depends on our ability to adapt to these rapidly changing technologies, align our services with evolving industry standards, and continually improve the know-how of our staff in response to the evolving demands of the marketplace. We are engaged in brokering and providing fintech services to our customers, and the success of the business hinges on our ability to continue adapting to evolving technology and finding our edge in the market. Staying ahead of technological advancements and integrating innovative solutions into our services is crucial for maintaining our competitive position. Failure to adapt to technological changes and effectively adopt new technology could result in a loss of market share and adversely affect our business, financial condition, and results of operations.","section":"Factors Affecting Our Results of Operations","block":15,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ff08f75f2fe5fe10b333696fe5e07677279dd4067d7354554b9c4bb27ff91ae6.bin","sha256":"ff08f75f2fe5fe10b333696fe5e07677279dd4067d7354554b9c4bb27ff91ae6"}},{"id":"6a85fa9ea3b4c4676cae8249c92a1272b0f75dc8befda41a5a411c1f82ec0dd4","quote":"We materially rely on our experienced employees to provide reliable and quality consultancy services to our customers, and believe that our experienced employees have developed strong relationships with our customers through their ability to provide personalized services through understanding customers’ needs. In addition to maintaining relationships with existing customers, we also rely on them to generate businesses with new customers. There is however no guarantee that our experienced employees will or are willing to continue to serve us. Where they determine to cease their employments with us or enter into negotiations with us for a material variation of their existing terms of employments, our operating performance and financial results may be materially and adversely affected.","context":"Our ability to retain employees who have strong relationships with our customers","section":"Factors Affecting Our Results of Operations","block":16,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ff08f75f2fe5fe10b333696fe5e07677279dd4067d7354554b9c4bb27ff91ae6.bin","sha256":"ff08f75f2fe5fe10b333696fe5e07677279dd4067d7354554b9c4bb27ff91ae6"}},{"id":"7e9ff27ff30877fde71fa7b9f139820bb27a59459d2d9bb025bd27e53709a190","quote":"We are currently facing intense market competition. Some of our current or potential competitors have significantly more financial, technical, marketing and other resources than we do and may be able to devote greater resources to the development, promotion and support of their customer acquisition and retention channels. In light of the low barriers to entry in the industry, we expect more players to enter this market and increase the level of competition. Our ability to differentiate our services from other competitors will have significant impact on our business growth in the future.","context":"Our business faces strong market competition","section":"Factors Affecting Our Results of Operations","block":18,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ff08f75f2fe5fe10b333696fe5e07677279dd4067d7354554b9c4bb27ff91ae6.bin","sha256":"ff08f75f2fe5fe10b333696fe5e07677279dd4067d7354554b9c4bb27ff91ae6"}},{"id":"156ac8c9fe9deb5aa504681ace6bdd093df24133ec4cd72619d22b5e71b4460b","quote":"The regulatory environment for the corporate and industrial park related services in Mainland China and Macau from time to time is evolving in order to govern the related sector. We have been closely tracking the development and implementation of new rules and regulations likely to affect us. We will continue to ensure timely compliance with any new rules and regulations and believe that such timely compliance is essential to our growth. To the extent that we may be required to adapt our operations to new laws and regulations, our operating costs may increase which will impact our profitability.","context":"Changes in the Mainland China and Macau Regulatory Environment may impact our business and results of operations","section":"Changes in the Mainland China and Macau Regulatory Environment may impact our business and results of operations","block":20,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-037914","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-14","reportDate":"2026-03-31","cik":"0002011458","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2011458/000149315226037914/ex99-1.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ff08f75f2fe5fe10b333696fe5e07677279dd4067d7354554b9c4bb27ff91ae6.bin","sha256":"ff08f75f2fe5fe10b333696fe5e07677279dd4067d7354554b9c4bb27ff91ae6"}},{"id":"009a447ccacd48f3db7f76651f0fd2a7488226cacd4610c0a253f80463f8280c","quote":"Our revenues consist of administrative services fees, fintech services fees, investment brokerage fees, project research fees and interest income and others. The foll